      "magnitude": "Annual A/E std dev ~0.34 vs expected sampling noise ~0.03-0.045; A/E swings from 0.613 to 1.653 while overall TPD A/E remains ~1.005",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "evidence": [
        "artifacts/ae_tpd_by_year.csv shows extreme annual A/E values: 0.793, 0.619, 0.613, 1.262, 0.759, 0.914, 1.653, 0.733, 1.073, 1.237.",
        "Expected TPD claim counts of 487 to 1,130 imply year-to-year Poisson noise in A/E of roughly 0.03-0.045, much smaller than the observed excursions.",
        "Overall TPD A/E is close to baseline (1.005), and the large moves appear in both directions rather than as a sustained level shift."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate TPD experience for data-quality or selection issues: reconcile actual claim counts, expected claims, exposure, coding, duration mix, duplicates, and any reporting changes. Decompose by age/gender and any available cause/diagnosis dimensions. Unless a cause is identified, do not change the central TPD A/E, but consider a higher volatility allowance/IBNR margin and close monitoring."
    }
  ]
}

